          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>How much does an Echelon treadmill cost?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On Echelon’s store on 26 November 2026, the Stride-6 was $1,399.99, the Stride-6s $1,599.99, the Stride 50 RCX-22 $1,999.99 and the Stride-8s $2,195.99, against compare-at prices of $1,999.99 to $2,999.99. Echelon’s walking pads were $299.99 (DuoPad) and $399.99 (DuoTread).
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much is the Echelon membership for a treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Echelon Premier was $39.99 a month after a 30-day free trial, $399.99 for a year or $699.99 for two years on Echelon’s treadmill pages on 26 November 2026. The yearly and two-year plans include free shipping on the treadmill. Over five years Premier costs about $1,800 to $2,400.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you use an Echelon treadmill without a membership?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes. Echelon’s Stride-6 page says no membership is needed to run and manual workouts from the console always work, and the Stride-8s page says Freestyle mode and built-in programs are always available. Without Premier you lose the classes, scenic and gamified content, and the five-year parts and labour cover.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does Echelon charge for delivery?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The Stride-8s includes delivery in the continental US with or without a membership. On the Stride-6, Stride-6s and Stride 50 RCX-22, shipping is free with a 1- or 2-year Premier plan; otherwise Echelon says rates are calculated at checkout. Premium in-home delivery and setup is $299.99 where available.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty comes with an Echelon treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For Stride treadmills bought on or after 4 November 2026, Echelon lists a lifetime motor warranty for the original purchaser, 10 years on the frame, 2 years on parts and 1 year on labour. Active Premier members get parts and labour extended to five years in total.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is Echelon cheaper than Peloton?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Usually, once the membership is counted. In Black Friday 2026 sales, the Stride-6s was $1,599.99 against $1,995 for Peloton’s Tread Flex, and Premier’s yearly plan costs about $1,000 less over five years than All-Access at $49.99 a month. The Stride-8s costs about $200 more to buy than a Tread Flex but about $800 less over five years.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the Echelon treadmill cheaper on Amazon?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Sometimes. On 26 November 2026 Amazon matched Echelon on the Stride-6 at $1,399.99 and was cheaper on the Stride-8s ($1,999.99) and DuoTread ($299.99). The Amazon Stride-8s listing states a 300 lb capacity against 400 lb on Echelon’s current model, and Echelon only accepts returns on items bought from echelonfit.com.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

